'' A DIM SHARED IS ONE MODULE'S OBJECT, and LLVM's 'internal' is what says so -- C's
'' 'static', which is what fbc writes. Emitted external, two modules that each declared
'' one were 'lld-link: error: duplicate symbol: e' where fbc compiles both; the same for
'' a 'private sub' holding a 'static'. See the source for fbc's measured table.
''
'' NOT ASSERTED HERE, because the harness compiles one file: the two-module programs.
'' Those were run against fbc by hand and their output matched byte for byte.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/shared-linkage.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"sh" = internal global
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"stsh" = internal global
'' A STATIC LOCAL IS NOBODY ELSE'S EITHER, and it is the shape a 'private sub' in two
'' modules collides on.
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"P$sl" = internal global
'' AND THE THREE OTHER MODULES ARE ENTITLED TO REACH KEEP THEIR LINKAGE. Marking any of
'' these internal is the same bug pointing the other way: a reference from another
'' module would not resolve.
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"cm" = global
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1T4CNT$E" = global
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"E$" = global
'' EXPECT-NOT: @"cm" = internal
'' EXPECT-NOT: @"E$" = internal
